Package: L1000PAI
Title: Direction-Aware Perturbation Activity Inference from Ranked
    Transcriptomic Signatures
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yilin", "Chiu", , "yilin1107@mail.ndmutsgh.edu.tw", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Infers the activity of genes and compounds from a ranked
    transcriptomic signature by comparing it with paired Up/Down perturbation
    signatures, such as the LINCS L1000 CRISPR knockout and chemical
    perturbation consensus libraries. Each arm is tested by preranked gene set
    enrichment analysis, and a directional intersection-union test requires
    both arms to support the same direction before an activity call is made.
    Single-signature libraries, covariance-aware joint scoring from
    synchronized null draws, sample-level scoring and versioned compound
    annotations are also provided, with helpers that turn ExpressionSet-based
    differential expression results into ranked inputs. Plotting functions
    draw the calls, their two arms and the pathways enriched among the
    Activated and the Inhibited targets, ready to present. A single call,
    pai_deg_report(), turns a differential-expression table into a PDF
    report written for non-specialists and an Excel workbook of every table
    behind it.
